body:
I've been looking forward to this PR for a long time and really hope it can be merged into the official Godot repo soon.

I've tried out this feature and found a few issues. Since the feature repo doesn't have an issues page, I'm bringing them up here for discussion – hope that's okay.

1. After opening the editor and trying to create a Resource in the FileSystem panel, custom Resources included via PackageReference don't show up in the list unless I rebuild the project in MSBuild panel. I spent some days digging into this and found the root cause: at some point during Godot's startup, [EditorFileSystem::_remove_invalid_global_class_name](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/editor/file_system/editor_file_system.cpp#L1672) calls [ScriptServer::remove_global_class](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/core/object/script_language.cpp#L443), which removes custom Resources that are multi-assembly scripts(their paths start with `"csharp://"`). As a result, when [CreateDialog::_fill_type_list()](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/editor/gui/create_dialog.cpp#L93) runs, it can't find those Resources, so they don't appear in the list.

2. [static void _register_csharp_global_class()](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/modules/mono/csharp_script.cpp#L2226) is called quite early during Godot startup (in [Main::setup2()](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/main/main.cpp#L2981)), before [EditorNode::get_singleton()](https://github.com/matelq/godot/blob/58520950da5e1a71f76930507c8ac635275f81d5/modules/mono/csharp_script.cpp#L2235) has been initialized. As a result, the following lines are not called.
``` c++
		if (EditorNode::get_singleton()) {
			EditorNode::get_editor_data().script_class_set_icon_path(p_type_info.class_name, p_type_info.icon_path);
			EditorNode::get_editor_data().script_class_set_name(p_script_path, p_type_info.class_name);
		}
```

I'm not sure if this causes other issues.


Note about point 1: I can't work around this by rebuilding my project, Because each rebuild triggers the well-known Issue: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/78513
